WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.168
-We're back with Chris Tucker.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.669
Obviously,
you came from stand-up.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:05.471
You talked about
making the leap to movies.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.039
They were,
in the beginning, comedies.

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:09.308
And then you've been great
in dramas, as well.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:10.810
You've worked with people --
like you said, Tarantino,

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.178
David O. Russell.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.247
And "Air." You were so fantastic
in the air this year.

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:16.949
-Thank you.
Thank you, thank you.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:18.651
It was awesome.
-And I didn't realize

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.486
the character you played,
Howard White...

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:22.488
-Yeah.
-...he wasn't originally

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:24.857
going to be in the script.
-No. No.

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:27.059
What happened was Ben Affleck
went down to talk

00:00:27.059 --> 00:00:28.894
with Michael Jordan to get
his blessings pretty much,

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.097
and say, "If you don't
want me to do this movie,
I won't do it."

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.231
Michael said, "I don't care.

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:33.632
Just, if you're gonna do
a movie about Nike,

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.068
you've got to have
Howard White in there

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:38.204
because Howard White
was my connection to Nike."

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:39.872
And then he tried -- he wanted

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.374
to find somebody
to play Howard White,

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.876
and he always said
he wanted to work with me.

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.144
By passing --
We would pass each other.

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:47.780
And we were looking
for something, my team.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:50.417
And Ben came to us, and he said,
"It's not a big part,

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:52.218
but you can do
whatever you want to do."

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:54.353
So I said, "Wait a minute.
I know Howard White."

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:55.788
So I called my --
He's my friend.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.491
I called Howard. He said, "Yeah,
I heard about this movie."

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:00.359
And he took me
through his whole life,

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.295
you know, back
to high-school teachers,

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.397
gym teachers, and principals
and all this stuff.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.365
So I just got
all this information,

00:01:06.365 --> 00:01:08.368
and I pretty much wrote
my own part in the movie.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:11.037
Like, six scenes.
I wrote every word in the movie,

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:12.738
my parts, and made it work.

00:01:12.738 --> 00:01:14.941
It was already a great script,

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.342
and I just made myself
work in there, so, yeah.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.043
-I mean,
what a great call by Affleck.

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.745
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Oh, yeah.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:23.015
-I mean,
for Affleck to cast you,

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:25.184
not realizing you know
the guy you're gonna play

00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:27.186
and then getting
free script writing.

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:28.821
-Yeah.
That's right. That's right.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:31.290
-He's a very, very smart man.
-He's a smart man, yeah.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.026
-I also know that one
of the reasons you knew Howard

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:36.095
is he was very helpful for you
over the years.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.197
He would donate stuff
to your charity auction.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.432
-Every year. It's crazy.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.033
That's why I say
that was a godsent role.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.468
Because every year
I would call him

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.969
for my foundation
golf tournament.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:45.704
We had the
Chris Tucker Foundation,

00:01:45.704 --> 00:01:47.273
and we raised money to do

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.041
underprivileged kids
scholarships

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.676
and homeless ministry
with our church.

00:01:50.676 --> 00:01:52.411
[ Cheers and applause ]
We do everything.

00:01:52.411 --> 00:01:54.814
So if you do good,
a movie role might come to you.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.816
A blessing will come to you.
Because I called him every year.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.184
And we kept in touch.
And I called him.

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.852
He said, "You want some more
shirts or something?"

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.454
I said, "No."
He didn't say that.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.189
But I was like, "No, man.
They're doing this movie,
and you in it.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.924
And they want me to play you."
He was like, "What?"

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:06.259
Then he took me down
this whole road.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:08.794
But, you know,
Viola Davis is in the movie.

00:02:08.794 --> 00:02:10.897
Chris Messina. Marlon Wayans.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.032
Jason Bateman.
Ben Affleck and Matt.

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:14.867
But I was scared
with Viola Davis

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:16.836
because Viola Davis
is a trained actor.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.371
She studied at Juilliard.
-Yes.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.207
-So the first scene, I was kind
of scared and I blacked out.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.675
I thought I --
I'm serious.

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.177
I thought I was in
the movie "The Help."

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.311
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:26.812
I looked her dead in the eyes

00:02:26.812 --> 00:02:28.848
and said, "You is kind...

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:33.018
you is smart...
and you is important."

00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:34.687
She said, "Chris,
what is wrong with you?!

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.089
This is not the movie
'The Help'!

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.823
-Yeah.
-Come on, now. Hurry up.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.492
Get yourself together!"
-Unusable take.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.795
-Yeah. "You're not in that
movie. This is 'Air.'

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.131
I got another movie
I gotta go do.

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:47.800
You the one who wait every five
years for your new movie."

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.835
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:52.038
-Man, it must be so exciting
to be about to get back

00:02:52.038 --> 00:02:53.940
on the stage this weekend
in New York City.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.241
Do you have
any backstage nerves

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.043
or is it just excitement
about getting out there

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.511
in front of people?
-Yeah, you get it,

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.480
but you learn how to control
your nerves, you know?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.581
And that's the best thing about
it because you master it.

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:03.750
Because every night, you know

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.384
it's a different audience,
different vibe,

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.785
and you just master it
and you say,

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:08.121
you know,
when you get out there,

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.655
you know,
the audience love you already.

00:03:09.655 --> 00:03:11.657
All you got to do is go out
there, relax, and have fun.

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.260
So that's what I do.
And the audience is great.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.495
It's great.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.931
-When you're on the road,
I'm sure there's still

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:20.633
new material occurring to you.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.267
Do you get excited
when you come up with something

00:03:22.267 --> 00:03:24.203
where you're like, "Oh, I think
I might have a new bit here"?

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:25.838
-Yeah, like, you know,
it's a muscle, man.

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:28.073
Once you get it going,
it don't stop, you know?

00:03:28.073 --> 00:03:30.109
You can make anything funny
once you --

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.610
if you got that that gift, man.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.880
And, yeah, I love it because
every day is something,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.015
and you add it onto something,
and it's in the moment.

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.850
It's live. It's like
being at the Super Bowl

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.185
and watching it on TV.
-Yeah.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.553
-In the moment and live
is just --

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.988
It's awesome
because the audience --

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:44.089
Somebody coming in late,
they might say something,

00:03:44.089 --> 00:03:46.258
and then there you go,
off on a whole nother thing.

00:03:46.258 --> 00:03:48.994
-Are you then happy a little bit
when someone comes in late?

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:50.430
So you have material?
-Sometimes.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.565
You know, sometimes
I'd rather just do the show,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.333
but, you know,
when something happens,

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.669
it just brings the best
out of me, I guess, you know?

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.771
-I think people also love
that moment where they're like,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.940
"oh, I'm seeing a thing now
that nobody else gets to see."

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.142
-Yeah. Oh, yeah. Nothing
like it. Nothing like it.

00:04:03.142 --> 00:04:05.177
-I know a lot of people
ask me all the time --

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.579
Will there be a "Rush Hour 4"?

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.747
Is this something that people
can expect an answer for

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:10.182
if they buy a ticket
to see you on stage?

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:11.784
-Yeah, I tell everybody,
you know, if you want to know

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.586
if I'm doing another
"Rush Hour 4" or "Friday,"

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.521
you got to come
to the Beacon Theatre.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.623
Saturday night,
because Friday night's sold out.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.191
-Friday is sold out.
-Come on out.

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:20.826
I think we got a few tickets
Saturday night.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.995
-All on my tour. You can catch
me anywhere around the world.

00:04:22.995 --> 00:04:25.898
St. Louis. Chicago.
I'm going all over.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.700
Indianapolis, We're everywhere.
-Well, look.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:29.134
Go check it out, you guys.

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:31.070
It is --
There it is right there.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.707
The Legend Tour 2023.
Chris Tucker, everybody.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.176
For tour information,
go to ChrisTucker.com.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:39.412
We'll be right back
with Paul Dano.

